WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:14.000
Our aim is to minimize J of theta. Theta is the parameter and J is the objective.

00:14.000 --> 00:30.000
The gradient gives the local direction of steepest increase of a differentiable objective.

00:30.000 --> 00:45.000
We update theta by subtracting alpha times the gradient of J at the current theta. Alpha is a positive learning rate.

00:45.000 --> 01:00.000
For J of theta equals theta squared, start at theta equals two. The derivative is two theta, so the gradient here is four.

01:00.000 --> 01:14.000
With alpha equal to one tenth, the next theta is two minus point four, or one point six.

01:14.000 --> 01:30.000
An excessive learning rate can overshoot. The useful step size depends on the shape of the objective.
